<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonel Fernández</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonel Fernández is a Dominican politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-liberation-party">Dominican Liberation Party</a> who served as president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> from 1996 to 2000 and again from 2004 to 2012. His governments promoted economic liberalisation, tourism and infrastructure, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> metro, during a period of rapid growth. He later founded the People's Force party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonel-fernandez.jpg" alt="Leonel Fernández" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agencia de Noticias ANDES · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reuni%C3%B3n_de_expresidentes_(27782591751)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
